From 03bf2c1e8a18769f6326a35017cf200185df25a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:02:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] make the three project surfaces one surface: shared table
 parts, the Projekte KPI row, and editable Gewerk rows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous patch gave BVB-EEA and PSV-ITK a workspace of their own. This
makes it the *same* workspace: the KPI row, the table chrome and the row
actions are now one implementation the three tabs import, rather than three
that happen to look alike today and would not have looked alike for long.

KPI row. Both Gewerk tabs now render the Projekte four-card row — same
grid, same accent on the first card, same 4xl figure, same 12px caption,
same colours. The figures come from deriveProjectMetrics, the derivation
Projekte and the Dashboard already share, called with each project's
reviews narrowed to the one department. "Aktiv", "Abgeschlossen" and
"Blockiert" therefore mean on /bvb-eea exactly what they mean on
/projects, because it is the same code deciding — not a second count that
drifts.

One label is deliberately not copied. Projekte counts every project, so
its "Gesamtprojekte 1.298" is exactly what that number is. The Gewerk tabs
count the projects carrying that Prüfung — 814 for EEA, 510 for ITK — and
labelling that "Gesamtprojekte" would state a total the dataset
contradicts. The card reads "Projekte mit EEA-Prüfung" and is otherwise
identical.

Table. Both Gewerk tables carry the full Projekte column set: sticky Nr.,
sortable Projektnummer / Region / Station / Bhf-Nr. / Strecken-Nr. /
Projektstand / Projektleiter / Termin PV, Beschreibung, then this Gewerk's
Prüfer, Prüfdatum and Status, then the actions column. Sorting is German
collation with dates compared as dates — sorting the rendered dd.mm.yyyy
as text ordered the column by day-of-month — and empty cells sink in both
directions instead of burying the rows a reader wants.

The rows are editable, which is what "changing names" in the audit
requirement actually needs. Projektnummer, Station, Projektstand,
Projektleiter, the Gewerk's Prüfer and its Status all write through the
same optimistic, rolled-back, audited mutations Projekte uses, because
applyEdit/applyReviewEdit moved out of useProjects into useProjectEdits.
They were trapped inside the filter-and-sort pipeline, so a page that only
wanted to edit a row had to take on the whole thing — which is why these
tables were read-only in the first place.

Shared parts, in client/src/components/workspace/table-parts.tsx:
InlineEditCell, SortHeader, ProjectCommentDialog and RowActions. Projects.tsx
now imports all four instead of defining its own; the Kommentar-und-Link
dialog it had inline is a component both surfaces mount.

Sort headers gained an explicit name. "Station, Schaltfläche" told a
screen-reader user nothing about what pressing it does, and the column also
holds 511 editable cells whose accessible names start with the same word —
the header was indistinguishable from its own column. It is now "Nach
Station sortieren"; aria-sort still reports the direction.

Independence is asserted, not assumed: a search and a view mode set on
BVB-EEA must not be visible on PSV-ITK, must not survive a return to
BVB-EEA, and the two tabs must not render the same row count.

Gates: tsc clean, biome unchanged at 72 pre-existing warnings, 174 unit
tests, build clean, e2e 52/52 (15 new), check-ui clean across 6 routes x
6 scenarios x 3 viewports x 4 theme combinations.
